Final warning texts (each prefixed "WARN " in the log, "unreagent: WARN " on stderr when the log is a file):
A interactive, claudeIntegration, allow_all: permissions are not enforced: the agent runs interactively in window mode (agent.window: true, or agent.window unset and no -p/--print in agent.args), and the launcher passes --permission-prompt-tool only to a headless agent, so permissions.mode (allow_all), allow and deny are never consulted. The launcher passes --dangerously-skip-permissions instead (mode allow_all): every tool call runs without a prompt, including one a deny rule names. To enforce the policy, run the agent headless: put "-p" (or "--print") and its task in agent.args, and leave agent.window unset or false.
B interactive, claudeIntegration, allowlist/deny_all: permissions are not enforced: the agent runs interactively in window mode (agent.window: true, or agent.window unset and no -p/--print in agent.args), and the launcher passes --permission-prompt-tool only to a headless agent, so permissions.mode (allowlist), allow and deny are never consulted. The launcher passes no permission flag instead: Claude Code asks in its window as usual, and you answer each prompt yourself. To enforce the policy, run the agent headless: put "-p" (or "--print") and its task in agent.args, and leave agent.window unset or false.
C interactive, claudeIntegration, hand-wired, allow_all: permissions are not enforced: the agent runs interactively in window mode (agent.window: true, or agent.window unset and no -p/--print in agent.args), and the --permission-prompt-tool wired into agent.args by hand takes effect only for a headless agent, so permissions.mode (allow_all), allow and deny are never consulted. The launcher also passes --dangerously-skip-permissions (mode allow_all). To enforce the policy, run the agent headless: put "-p" (or "--print") and its task in agent.args, and leave agent.window unset or false.
D interactive, hand-wired, any other case (claudeIntegration true with allowlist/deny_all, or claudeIntegration false with any mode): as C without the sentence "The launcher also passes --dangerously-skip-permissions (mode allow_all)."
F interactive, claudeIntegration false, not hand-wired: permissions are not enforced: agent.claudeIntegration is false, so the launcher passes the agent no --permission-prompt-tool and permissions.mode (allow_all), allow and deny are never consulted. To enforce the policy, set agent.claudeIntegration: true (Claude Code only) and run the agent headless: put "-p" (or "--print") and its task in agent.args, and leave agent.window unset or false.
G headless, claudeIntegration false, not hand-wired: as F, ending "To enforce the policy, set agent.claudeIntegration: true (Claude Code only)."

